WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:03.420
- [Narrator] Solaris,
Galactica Super Nova,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.670
and the Flying Fox.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.740
These multimillion dollar superyachts

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.840
in this idyllic Turkish port

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.060
are linked to Russian oligarchs.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.960
While several vessels have been
seized by the US and the EU,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.810
tracking experts say
these yachts are in Turkey

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.780
because the country isn't
imposing sanctions on them,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.780
and intelligence analysts say
the boats are taking measures

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.430
to slip off the radar.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.890
- They were turning off
their tracking systems

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.370
so it also became sort
of an international hunt.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.020
- [Narrator] This former CIA officer

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.780
and other internet sleuths
have made it their mission

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.070
to track them down.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.040
- These boats can't
stay out forever, right?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.720
- [Narrator] So as
authorities around the world

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.880
are chasing down the sanctioned assets,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.620
here's how intelligence analysts

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.740
are using vessel tracking
data, satellite images,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.113
and on the ground sources
to help find them.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.870
In early February, just
before Russia invaded Ukraine,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.300
some superyachts linked
to Russian oligarchs

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.340
were docked in Barcelona, Spain.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.870
Although definitions vary,

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.790
marine experts say superyachts

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.010
are usually over 80 feet long,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.460
while megayachts can span over 200 feet.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.620
- You could go down to
the Port of Barcelona

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.130
and see really a dozen or so, at least,

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.360
super and megayachts.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.950
Not all of them were Russian, of course,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.630
but a lot of them were.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.900
- [Narrator] That's Alex
Finley, a former CIA officer.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.000
She began monitoring oligarch's yachts

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.830
while researching for a novel,

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.980
even before Russia launched
its invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.130
- I would go down to sort of
check the status of everything

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.210
and then very quickly,
as the invasion started,

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.550
we started seeing all
of these yachts take off

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.380
very quickly from here.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.500
- [Narrator] That includes
Solaris, a 460 foot megayacht

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.410
owned by Russian billionaire
Roman Abramovich.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.490
While it was in Spain,

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.490
it could have been seized
under international sanctions.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.020
- I was watching her regularly
to see when she might flee.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.470
Just before sanctions came
down on Roman Abramovich,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.680
about 36 hours before those
sanctions were announced,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.623
Solaris did in fact leave Barcelona.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.980
- [Narrator] To try to find
out where the yacht went,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.870
Finley and other open source analysts

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.760
use a tool called MarineTraffic.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.430
It collects tracking
information from ships and boats

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.983
from all over the globe
using a system called AIS.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.100
That works by collecting
a transponder signal

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.740
that's represented by
this yellow line here.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.160
Data show on March 8th,
Solaris set off from Barcelona,

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.710
traveled over a thousand nautical miles,

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:35.520
and four days later, arrived
off the coast of Montenegro.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.613
Tracking information later
pinged its location in Turkey.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.940
Other vessels owned by
sanctioned oligarchs

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.730
made similar journeys
but were harder to track.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.620
That's because their AIS signals

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.320
stopped reporting a live location.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.110
One of them is Galactica Super Nova.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.570
The vessel is owned by Vagit Alekperov.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.150
That's according to the
website Superyacht Fan

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.230
and a former crew member

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.270
who spoke to "The Wall Street Journal."

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.300
The Galactica Super Nova
also ended up in Montenegro

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.340
after leaving from Barcelona,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.850
but then, its tracking signal
disappeared from the site,

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.400
so analysts had to look
elsewhere for information

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.633
on its whereabouts.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.890
In these cases, they
turned to a low tech tool,

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.600
eyewitness accounts.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.140
Boat captains like Emrah
Akkoyun in Gocek, Turkey,

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.224
can notice new arrivals.

00:03:24.224 --> 00:03:27.474
(Emrah speaks Turkish)

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.660
Intelligence analysts that
track open source data

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.160
say that firsthand sources,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.550
including local fishermen
and Turkish boat operators,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.830
can also help them monitor the yachts.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.487
- Somebody in Turkey can say,

00:03:45.487 --> 00:03:47.460
"Hey, we just spotted
this particular yacht,"

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.720
and they can send you a photo

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.540
and you have verification
that those things are there.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.730
- [Narrator] Locals in Gocek
have been sharing pictures

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.400
on social media and have
proactively sent information

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.260
to internet sleuths.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.560
Both Galactica Super Nova and
Solaris have been spotted here

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.900
in this Turkish port by eyewitnesses

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.760
who spoke to "The Wall Street Journal."

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.500
Intelligence analysts say the country

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.210
has allowed sanctioned vessels

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.193
to have safe haven in its ports.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.770
Turkey is the only NATO member

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.690
to have not imposed financial sanctions

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.400
on Russian oligarchs.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.870
Signaling instead that it wanted

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.883
to increase cooperation with Russia.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.210
On the ground, residents say

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.980
there has been a noticeable surge

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.170
of Russian-linked superyachts in the area

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.040
since the conflict began.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.290
(Kenan speaks Turkish)

00:04:44.716 --> 00:04:47.460
Some of these yachts are
also just too big to hide

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.900
from the eyes in the sky.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.160
Satellites.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.630
Take the Flying Fox,

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.120
which was once the largest yacht available

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.500
for public charter.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.230
It can be seen here in satellite imagery.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.650
The vessel is linked to Russian
oligarch Dmitry Kamenshchik,

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.350
according to the Superyacht
Fan base website.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.600
Flying Fox was added to the sanctions list

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.570
as blocked property by the US in June.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.000
That essentially means it can be seized.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.280
Its management company, Imperial Yachts,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.803
was also sanctioned by
the same authorities.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.580
Just a few months before sanctions
were placed on the vessel

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:24.120
in late April, it traveled
away from the coast of Haiti.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.100
It sailed across the Atlantic Ocean

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.050
before arriving in Turkey.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.450
The journey was recorded by AIS data

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:33.603
and its location was corroborated
by satellite imagery.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.710
Satellites can virtually
help locate big objects

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.630
anywhere in the world.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.220
- With commercial satellite,

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.320
you can visually see from above,

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.210
so if you get a hint or a clue

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.580
that a yacht might be in a certain place,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.600
you can actually look it up

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.080
with commercial satellite
imagery to to verify that.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.250
- [Narrator] Those satellite photos

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.400
have also helped analysts
find oligarch-linked boats

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.510
in the Middle East

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.550
where some vessels appear to have migrated

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.267
during the winter.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.450
"The Wall Street Journal"
reached out to Abramovich

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.770
about the movements of his yacht

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.720
but didn't receive a response.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.570
Kamenshchik and Alekperov
couldn't be reached.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.390
Imperial Yachts didn't respond
to a request for comment

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.763
and neither did Turkey and Montenegro.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.390
As internet sleuths bring more attention

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.560
to the vessels' movements,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.840
authorities are also
deploying new resources

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.190
to track them down.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.020
In the US, the Department of Justice

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.600
announced an initiative
called KleptoCapture

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.240
to both search for and seize the assets.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.060
- The task force is dedicated
to enforcing the sanctions,

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:36.120
export restrictions, and
economic countermeasures

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.680
that the United States has imposed,

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.500
along with its international
allies and partners,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.010
in response to this
unprovoked military invasion.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:44.843
- [Narrator] That's in addition

00:06:44.843 --> 00:06:48.180
to a transatlantic task force
led by the EU Commission

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.460
and other allied countries.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.030
But once the yachts, like
this one in Spain, are seized,

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.300
it's just the beginning
of a complex process.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.493
Namely the cost of maintaining them.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.270
Analysts say costs for
another impounded yacht,

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.560
this one in the US,

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.830
is estimated to be around
$10 million a year.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.510
Authorities are often paying the bill

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:11.760
to prevent the boats
from losing their value.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:15.840
The US has said it would look
to sell the seized yachts.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.320
However, it can be a long
and drawn out process,

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.293
leaving the fate of many of
these vessels up in the air.

